    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_092e61ec4e7524581f70bb3f16481f0c286d4a0011598adb4623faca9eb0861a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a continuous certification chain: verified RH below a fixed height and Kadiri's zero-free tail are matched to obtain the R=6.455 input; the adapted Schoenfeld argument turns that input into explicit theta/psi errors; partial summation then transports theta error to pi(x)-li(x), with an integral split separating asymptotic tail control from finite accounting and prime-breakpoint checks closing the remaining range.",
