      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c1c5f48f4c3e294681654a49a20186f3d03e81b7e486190682c2e9a409e24b06",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The explicit prime-distribution estimates function as modular inputs to several application-specific adapters rather than as one identical downstream proof: a nearby-prime width is substituted into an extremal arithmetic-progression argument, a reciprocal-log-squared theta target sets up short-interval positivity, and Theorem 1 replaces older analytic input in the P-integer bound and in the cited RH-qualified Ramanujan-inequality result.",
