    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_dde27e15719f6de66ceb07ca685849affddcd1118fd27ff48d5cbd4ce6ad3905",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source localizes optimization leverage by both dependency position and counterfactual sensitivity. It freezes B=17 to preserve inherited proof compatibility, observes that more gap data scarcely changes the short-interval constant while a smaller theta-error coefficient would, finds that even ideal secondary P-integer coefficients barely improve its threshold, and therefore points to the zero-free/psi/theta pipeline or a bespoke reconstruction of Schoenfeld's argument as more direct intervention sites.",
